# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, a checkout on Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# every text file to CRLF. That is harmless for Go sources, and fatal for
# anything a Linux shell has to run: a compose file whose inline Dockerfile
# writes an entrypoint hands the container a script whose lines end in \r, and
# the shell reports
#
#   /entrypoint.sh: 23: Syntax error: "fi" unexpected (expecting "then")
#
# because it read `then\r`, which is not `then`. The same applies to build.sh
# and to the systemd units and nginx config, which are read on the server.
#
# So: normalize everything to LF in the working tree, and make the exceptions
# explicit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Files that must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.syso binary
*.exe binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
